<title>SOUTH KOREA: Hanwha Chemical 1996 net turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Hanwha Chemical 1996 net turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	  (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			(loss)    476  vs (profit) 1,094</p>
<p>    Net				(loss)  25.68  vs (profit) 50.55</p>
<p>    Profit/Loss before tax     (loss)  24.97  vs (profit) 59.95</p>
<p>    Revenue				 1,534.26  vs     1,484.75</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	  Common	(in cash)   nil   vs  2</p>
<p>			  (in stock)  nil   vs  3</p>
<p>	  Preferred   (in cash)   nil   vs  2</p>
<p>			  (in stock)  nil   vs  3</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss			4.56  vs  3.71</p>
<p>NOTE: Net losses in 1996 were caused by a rise in world naphtha prices, a main raw material, while polyethylene and PVC product prices fell. The weakening won also added to the dollar denominated debt. --Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5648</p>
</text>
